  "literature_notes": "C-terminal tags (V5: L1/L2; eYFP: L3/L5/L7; SYFP2: L4; FLAG: L11/L12; EGFP component of L8; SmBiT: L13) are all placed at position 466, which falls within the intracellular C-terminal tail (ICL4: 396-466). These are tolerated and functionally silent (L12 shows EC50=2nM for GIP-stimulated cAMP), but they are cytoplasmic and therefore not extracellular surface tag sites; they are recorded in other_positions. L16 (HiBiT extracellular detection) implies an N-terminal extracellular tag but names no residue and no new position beyond what L6 already pins; it is not a separate site. L18 (Flag/HA by site-directed mutagenesis) names no residue or loop; the position cannot be pinned and the clip is dropped. No internal extracellular loop insertions are reported in the ledger for GIPR.",
